    public PaydayLoan(int loanAmount, int loanTerm, int interestRate) {
        this.loanAmount = loanAmount;
        this.loanTerm = loanTerm;
        this.interestRate = interestRate;
    }
}
```

With this rewritten code, the variable `interestRate` more accurately reflects its purpose, as it is no longer used to store a specific interest rate, but rather to store the total annual percentage of interest due to the high cost of lending.

